**[comments] Rule 4, comment lines that map to no code line: shorten**

Lines 61-62 restate the std::function type on lines 78-79, and lines 67-77 (the VNNI pair layout of K, the pair interleave of V, the AMX B-operand rationale and the reduction axes) map to no code line in gof.hpp and restate Note [K VNNI storage] (kv_cache.hpp; its item 4 already describes what k_head_fn and v_head_fn copy) and Note [VNNI Packed V layout] (v_vnni.hpp). The facts the type does not carry are the row unit, the scratch precondition (caller-owned, 64-byte-aligned, HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE bf16) and which buffer the result points into, so the proposal keeps those three facts plus one pointer to the Note; context lines 59-60 stay as they are.

Proposed:
```cpp
  // k_head_fn / v_head_fn return this token's K / V row for kv_head:
  // HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE bf16 values in dimension order. The caller passes a
  // 64-byte-aligned scratch of that size. The result points into the page when
  // the row is stored contiguously there, else into scratch, where the callback
  // rebuilt the row (which rows: Note [K VNNI storage] item 4, kv_cache.hpp).
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
L1 (k_head_fn / v_head_fn return this token's K / V row for kv_head) -> lines 78-79, the two members and their bf16* return. L2 (HW_BAKED_HEAD_SIZE bf16 values in dimension order) -> the bf16* return on 78-79: its length and element order. L3 (caller passes a 64-byte-aligned scratch of that size) -> the `bf16* scratch` parameter on 78-79: the precondition. L4-L5 (result points into the page or into scratch; Note pointer for which rows are rebuilt) -> the bf16* return on 78-79: which buffer it addresses and how long it stays valid.

