This is the paragraph the PR adds to Note [QK orientation]. Its lines 221-226 (block save through page::set_k_block, the row-major tail block, the in-place transpose at the forward end, the decode reason) repeat what Note [Row-major tail block] (h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp:437-456) and Note [K VNNI storage] (kv_cache.hpp:677-700) already say under the names the sentence cites. The orientation Note needs only the fact that the transpose cost moved to the K save, plus the pointer.

Proposed:
```cpp
// With TRON_K_VNNI (Note [K VNNI storage] in kv_cache.hpp) the stored K plane
// IS the VNNI B-operand layout. The orientation therefore flips. qk_vnni_128x4
// takes the 4 query rows, padded to 16 rows, as the A operand. The 16 K panels
// of the page are the B operand. The tiles come out as S[query][token]. No
// transpose is needed. The cost moves to the K save: a block is transposed
// once, at the block save or at the end of the forward pass that saved its
// 16th row (Note [Row-major tail block] in h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp). The
// software reader for the VNNI blocks of partial pages runs k_vnni::qk_group;
// the row-major tail block keeps the row-major dotter.
```

