```

**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

Three parts of this comment repeat text that lives elsewhere under a name the comment already cites. 'The padded Q rows are the A operand. The page's 16 K panels are the B operand. There is no transpose.' repeats the paragraph the PR adds to Note [QK orientation] (lines 218-221); a pointer suffices, as the qk_rowmajor_128x4 comment does. 'The 16-row tile stores write to a buffer inside the kernel. Only the 4 query rows are copied out.' is the mechanism behind the one contract fact (`s` needs 4 rows); it already sits at the code (amx_attn.cpp:245-247) and belongs in Note [Tile stores write 16 rows], which today names qk_rowmajor_128x4 only, so one clause there naming qk_vnni_128x4 would complete the Note. 'k_page = the page's packed K plane (64 tokens x 128 dims, 16 KiB, layout in h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp) as its typed view, so that a native K view, a packed V plane or a bare pointer cannot be handed in by mistake' restates the parameter type k_vnni_view<const bf16, PAGE_TOKENS_64, HEAD_SIZE_128>, whose own comment (k_vnni.hpp:161-163) states that it has no public pointer constructor and no pointer conversion; 16 KiB follows from 64 x 128 x 2 bytes.

