Proposed:
```cpp
// The AVX-512 (the CPU's 512-bit vector instruction set) QK score reader of the
// K VNNI layout (h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp). No AMX (Advanced Matrix Extensions,
// the tile instruction set) instruction runs here. So any translation unit may
// include it. The layout itself, who writes it and who reads it are described
// in Note [K VNNI storage] (in kv_cache.hpp).
//
// Words used here: bf16 is the 16-bit brain floating-point format. fp16 is the
// 16-bit IEEE half format. fp32 is the 32-bit IEEE single format. VDPBF16PS is
// the AVX-512 instruction that multiplies bf16 pairs and adds them in fp32.
```

**[comments] Rule 4, comment lines that map to no code line: shorten**

Of 25 lines, 9 survive: the output formula, the masked-store and masked-load contract, the layout precondition, the q stride, and the numerics class. Cut as caller context (Rule 4): "the caller keeps them at -inf" (self_attention.hpp:1950 does that) and "the caller scores the tokens of a row-major block with the row-major dotter and keeps their bits clear" (self_attention.hpp:2015-2025). Cut as restatements (Rule 2): the "Token lanes ... no horizontal reduction and no per-token gather" group repeats Note [K VNNI storage] item 3 and the intrinsics at lines 99-106 (the lane fact moves to the load comment at line 96); "k_page is the page's packed K plane as its typed view ... one of the two layout-specific readers allowed to take the plane address" repeats the parameter type and the k_vnni_access comment (tensor/k_vnni.hpp:145-149); "a group of more than 16 heads is scored 16 heads at a time" repeats lines 67-72, and its add-order sentence moves to the split at line 68; the bf16, float and fp16 paragraphs repeat the Words definition of VDPBF16PS, the intrinsics at lines 105-119 with the inline comment at 109-110, and the conversion loop at 74-78.

Proposed:
```cpp
// Scores of one query group against the live tokens of one page, read from
// the VNNI plane with AVX-512: s[h * s_stride + t] = q_h . K_t (UNSCALED) for
// every token t whose bit is set in `live`. Other entries of s are not
// written. The K storage of a token whose bit is clear is never read. It may
// be unwritten. Precondition: every block with a live bit holds the VNNI
// layout (Note [Row-major tail block] in h/tron/tensor/k_vnni.hpp). q points
// at kv_mul rows of 128 values (row stride 128). Numerics: the same products
// as the row-major dotter, added in fp32 in another order (Note [AMX
// attention dispatch]).
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
lines 1-3 (output formula, UNSCALED, live mask) -> line 87 (mask = live >> c*16) and line 125 (_mm512_mask_storeu_ps to s + h*s_stride + c*16); lines 3-4 "Other entries of s are not written" -> line 125 (mask store); lines 4-5 "K storage ... never read. It may be unwritten." -> line 99 (_mm512_maskz_loadu_epi32(mask, ...)); lines 5-6 precondition -> line 94 (panel address assumes the VNNI panel formula); lines 6-7 q stride -> lines 104, 117, 119 (q + h * HEAD_SIZE_128 + d); lines 7-9 numerics -> line 105 (_mm512_dpbf16_ps) and lines 116-119 (_mm512_fmadd_ps)

